description:
[claude] Owner, 2026-11-05: the juniors get the codebase tomorrow morning and must be able to point the factory at **their own project folder, in whatever shape or form**, not only a GitHub repo.

ANVIL-55 (#74) handles one shape: a git working copy at an absolute path with no spaces, on the branch the ticket names. Gaps found on main:

* **a plain folder** (no `.git`) is refused;
* **UI sessions hardcode **`base_ref="main"` (`app.py` `create_run`), so a repo on `master` or any other branch fails;
* **paths with spaces** are refused, and the ticket's `Code base:` line can't express them;
* `.zip` / `.tar.gz` archives are not accepted;
* **uncommitted changes** in a working copy are silently ignored;
* **folder names** outside `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]` are refused.

**Design:** the host normalises any source into the same thing #74 already ships, a shallow single-branch `.git`.

* **Git working copy:** as today, but the default base is the repo's **current branch** (UI and intake when no branch is given). Uncommitted changes are **reported** in the run record and the agent's task, and are not copied by default; an explicit opt-in snapshots them as one extra commit.
* **Plain folder:** the host makes a temporary git repo from it (one snapshot commit; respects a `.gitignore` if present, and skips `.git`, `node_modules`, `__pycache__`, `.venv`, `build/`), then continues as above. The patch and bundle apply to that snapshot.
* **Archive (**`.zip`, `.tar.gz`, `.tgz`): extracted safely (no absolute paths, `..` or links) into a temp folder, then treated as a plain folder.
* **Any path, including spaces:** the path is only ever used in host `subprocess` argument lists, never in a shell. The sandbox directory name is a sanitised slug of the folder name. Tickets may quote the path: `Code base: branch main of "C:\My Projects\app"`, and the branch is optional.

**Acceptance:**

* tests for each shape (plain folder, archive, a repo on `master` with no branch given, a path with spaces, a working copy with uncommitted changes reported);
* an end-to-end run in the real sandbox for a plain folder, with its patch applying back with `git apply`;
* SETUP.md documents the shapes.

comments.body:
[claude] Done: PR #94 merged (9e68e01), reviewed and re-approved by devin.

Acceptance met (`backend/tests/test_local_shapes.py`):

* **One test per shape:**

  * plain folder snapshot (junk excluded; folder never written);
  * `.gitignore` respected;
  * zip and tar.gz;
  * zip-slip refused;
  * a repo on `master` with no branch given → `master`, with 2 uncommitted changes reported and the committed base copied;
  * GitHub sessions still `main`;
  * five ticket-line forms, including a quoted path with spaces and no branch.
* **End to end in the real sandbox** (`test_plain_folder_with_spaces_end_to_end`): a plain folder at `My Projects\Sensor App` → `/workspace/Sensor-App` → commit → patch → `git apply` in the original folder.
* **Docs:** SETUP.md §5b and HANDOFF.md "Known limits" describe the shapes.

Full suite at the PR: 346 passed. Devin rebuilds the junior zip from this main (ANVIL-92).
